===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|en|broke|er|id2=comparative}}.

====Adjective====
{{head|en|comparative adjective}}

# {{en-comparative of|broke}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|broker}}, {{m|enm|brokour}}, {{m|enm|brocour}}, from {{der|en|xno|brocour||small trader}} (compare also {{m|fro|abroker||to act as a broker}}), from {{der|en|odt|*brokere||one who determines the usages of trade, manager}}, from {{m|odt|broke}}, {{m|odt|bruyck}}, {{m|odt|breuck||use, usage, trade}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*brūkī||use, custom}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*brūkiz||use, custom}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-||to use, enjoy}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|brook|er|id2=agent noun}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|gml|brukere||a broker}}, {{cog|da|bruger||a broker, user, handler}}, {{cog|sv|bruk||use, custom, trade, business}}, {{cog|ang|broc||use, profit, advantage, foredeal}}. Compare also {{cog|fr|brocanter||to deal in second-hand goods}} from the same Germanic source. More at {{m|en|brook}}. {{rel-bottom}}

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[mediator]] between a [[buyer]] and [[seller]].
#: {{hypo|en|playbroker|power broker|stockbroker|pawnbroker|floor broker|honest broker|money broker|piece broker|produce broker|sworn broker}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Francesca Carrara|page=119|volume=II|text=It is singular how forcibly this passage in my narrative brings to my mind a picture which used to be, some years ago, at a '''broker''''s—that charnel-house of the comforts and graces of life. It had been taken out of its frame, and leant in a dark and dusty corner against a perpendicular armchair, whose rigid uprightness seemed suited only to the parlour of a dentist, repose being the last idea it suggested.}}
# A [[stockbroker]].
# A [[mediator]] in general, one who liaises between two or more parties to attempt to achieve an outcome of some kind.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Spencer C. Tucker|title=World War I: The Definitive Encyclopedia and Document Collection|isbn=1851099654|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=DBwTBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA243&dq=%22broker+of+peace%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwidudT68dnLAhXIGD4KHYJiCCwQ6AEIRzAF#v=onepage&q=%22broker%20of%20peace%22&f=false|page=244
|passage=The peace plan was representative of Benedict's inability to appear as a neutral '''broker''' of peace}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} An agent involved in the exchange of messages or transactions.
#: {{hypo|en|message broker|object request broker|storage resource broker|tunnel broker}}

